@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy — NEXUS";
    ViewData["BodyClass"] = "public-body";
}

@section Styles {
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/public-pages.css" />
}

<section class="pps-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="lead">
            What NEXUS collects when you apply for a connection, why we need it,
            and how long we keep it. </p> </div>
</section>

<section class="pps-section">
    <div class="container pps-prose">

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
            When you order a connection we record your name, CNIC, mobile number,
            email address and installation address. For a Dial-Up or Telephone
            line we also record the landline number, because the service runs
            over it. </p>
        <p>
            Once a line is live we keep the technical records needed to support
            it: the plan you are on, the exchange serving you, your connection
            history and the bills raised against the account. </p>

        <h2>Why we need it</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>To verify your identity before installing a line at an address.</li>
            <li>To run a feasibility survey against the exchange serving you.</li>
            <li>To raise bills and record payments against the correct account.</li>
            <li>To reach you about installation appointments and service faults.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who can see it</h2>
        <p>
            Access is limited by role. Field technicians see the part of your
            record needed to install and maintain the line. Accounts staff see
            billing records. Retail clerks see the records for orders they raise.
            Full access to an account is restricted to the administrator. </p>
        <p>
            We do not sell customer data and we do not share it with third
            parties for marketing. </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
            Billing and payment records are retained for as long as the account
            is open, and afterwards for the period required for financial audit.
            Orders that were never completed are kept so the survey history is
            not lost, but they are not linked to an active line. </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
            You can ask to see the record we hold on you, ask for a correction if
            something is wrong, or ask us to close your account. Requests should
            go to the customer service desk at your nearest NEXUS retail shop. </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
            Questions about this policy can be raised through the
            <a href="/Home/Contact">contact page</a>. </p> </div>
</section>
